# STIG CD16-00-000600: PostgreSQL must allow only the information system security m
# STIG ID: V-261862 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `pg16-cd16-00-000600-pgdata-owner-perms-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `pg16`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG CD16-00-000600: PostgreSQL must allow only the information system security manager (ISSM), or in`
    description `PostgreSQL must allow only the information system security manager (ISSM), or individuals or roles appointed by the ISSM, to select which events are to be audited.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `pg16,stig,disa-stig`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:CD16-00-000600,NIST-800-53:AU-12`
    control_objective `AU-12`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `dba`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `PostgreSQL16:localhost:pg-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA STIG guidance for CD16-00-000600.`

    component_id `comp-pg16-db`

    impl_AU_12 `This control is validated by checking the required PostgreSQL configuration against the DISA STIG baseline.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        path `/var/lib/pgsql/16/data`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE meta_check
        exists boolean = true
        permissions string = `0700`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN file_metadata
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF meta_check
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
